;; it-fencei.expected.sexp — the expected observations for `it-fencei.s` (P2-SCALAR.4).
;; Validate with:
;;   python3 scripts/check_sexp_schema.py it-fencei.expected.sexp schema/expectations.sexp

(comment "it-fencei.expected.sexp — the expected observations for `it-fencei.s`." "" "⛔ EVERY VALUE HERE WAS DERIVED FROM THE PINNED SPECIFICATION PROSE BEFORE THE PROGRAM WAS RUN" "(EVD-05), against the reference behaviors MEASURED by probe (P2-SCALAR.3): both references EXECUTE" "fence.i as a nop and CONTINUE, although their matched configurations exclude Zifencei — recorded" "as DIFF-FENCEI-EXECUTED in references.sexp. This profile declares Zifencei absent, so semulith" "reports the reserved encoding and the laboratory's declared D-RESERVED-DECODE policy converts it" "to the illegal-instruction observation, stopping the run. ⭐ The comparison is NOT disabled:" "(expect_divergence …) declares that it must diverge at EXACTLY step 1 — an AGREE verdict would be" "the RED case (a stale pin, not a good comparison). These expectations describe SEMULITH's two" "steps; x2 must NEVER be written by semulith (the continuation marker belongs to the references'" "longer runs).")
(expectations (program "it-fencei.s") (entry "0x80000000") (instructions 2) (never_written "x2") (expect_divergence (difference "DIFF-FENCEI-EXECUTED") (at_step 1)) (step (n 0) (insn "addi x1, x0, 1") (writes (write (reg "x1") (value "0x0000000000000001"))) (derivation "The agreeing prefix — an ordinary write all three models perform identically, so the divergence at the next step is attributable to the fence.i alone.") (source "RVI-RV32I §1.1.4")) (step (n 1) (insn ".word 0x0000100F") (writes) (derivation "0x0000100F is fence.i. Zifencei is absent from this profile, so the word matches no row of the generated decode table: a RESERVED instruction, whose behavior the architecture declares UNSPECIFIED. The laboratory's policy (D-RESERVED-DECODE) raises illegal-instruction with tval = the offending word: cause 0x02, tval 0x000000000000100F — and the run stops (Stop::Undefined keeps the source classification, SEM-07). Both references instead nop it and continue (measured) — the legitimate UNSPECIFIED divergence this guest's expect_divergence declaration pins.") (source "RVI-RV32I §1.1.5.2 (the reserved-instruction note: UNSPECIFIED) — decision D-RESERVED-DECODE; DIFF-FENCEI-EXECUTED (references.sexp)")))
